      },
      "summary": "The changed tests cover each behavioral acceptance criterion, including witness and digest validation, routing under incomplete or uncertain coverage, zero eligible examples, and literal, split, and encoded instructions. The named test file is exercised by the repository’s test command.",
      "findingList": []
    },
    {
      "agentId": "security-reviewer",
      "reviewType": "security",
      "harness": "codex",
      "harnessVersion": "0.162.0",
      "model": "gpt-6-luna",
      "approved": false,
      "findings": {
        "critical": 0,
        "major": 1,
        "minor": 0,
        "suggestion": 0
      },
      "summary": "A MissingRequirement claim can pass validation when its typed requirement is stated as signed off but an unrelated item in the same clause is pending. With complete coverage, that claim produces a request.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Investigation/ClaimValidator.cs",
          "line": 157,
          "message": "The open-gap check can attribute an unrelated pending item to the typed value when both appear in one clause. Require the open-gap statement to apply to the typed value before marking the claim supported.",
          "confidence": 0.9,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "For MissingRequirement claims, StatesOpenGap checks whether a clause contains both the typed value and any open-gap keyword. ClauseSplit does not separate clauses joined by conjunctions such as “and.” A supported claim is routed as a request when coverage is complete.",
            "failureScenario": "With complete coverage, a current witness says “Reserve approval is signed off and calibration is pending.” An investigator submits that quote as the claim, labels it MissingRequirement, and uses “Reserve approval” as the typed value. The clause contains both the typed value and “pending,” so validation marks it Supported and routing creates a request for reserve approval even though the quote says it is signed off. OWASP A08:2025."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
